## Objectives of the Project
This project aims to answer the following questions:
- What ideas about the cosmos and gods are shown by the way Daoist-folk temples arrange their deity statues? 
- Why do these temples include Buddhist figures, and how are those figures placed and displayed differently than in Chinese Buddhist temples? 
- What patterns can be seen when comparing altar setups across five Daoist-folk temples and two Chinese Buddhist temples? 

Three approaches to answer these questions: 
1. Textual analysis of Daoist, Buddhist, and folk religious texts
2. Photographic and ethnographic documentation on the altar arrangements in Singapore Chinese temples
3. Utilization of the Relational–Functional Iconographic Grammar (RFIG) to compare the arrangements systematically. 
The project repository here records data of the second and third approaches.
